  "description": "Determine if the given points form a convex polygon by checking the cross product orientation of consecutive edges.",
  "target": null,
  "pseudocode": "1. n = points.length\n2. prevCrossProduct = 0\n3. for i = 0 to n - 1:\n4.   p1 = points[i], p2 = points[(i+1)%n], p3 = points[(i+2)%n]\n5.   dx1 = p2[0]-p1[0], dy1 = p2[1]-p1[1]\n6.   dx2 = p3[0]-p2[0], dy2 = p3[1]-p2[1]\n7.   cp = dx1 * dy2 - dy1 * dx2\n8.   if cp != 0:\n9.     if (cp > 0 and prevCrossProduct < 0) or (cp < 0 and prevCrossProduct > 0) return false\n10.    prevCrossProduct = cp",
